@tabacitu 

There is a small issue I've been noticing as I used dark mode more and more. That is, even though the css provided by Tabler includes a list of color variables that we can adjust to achieve a Backpack look, it doesn't really do the trick (specially in dark mode). I know, a bummer. That is because there are lots of colors which are mixed when the css is compiled, e.g.: shadows colors, grays (gray-100, gray-200, gray-300...), and middle tones are not really properly set (even after setting the variable color). So what's the issue? Occasionally, I see blue colors in some parts of the page. very frustrating!

[Solution A] One quick fix is to override the colors by targeting the classes using css (tried to do that, but still, I keep discovering components that I haven't targeted).

[Solution B] The good solution (IMHO) is to compile the css using scss files provided by Tabler, and let Tabler do the right color mixing using Backpack color as primary (as well as success, danger, warning, etc, from Backstrap).

The good news?! I did compile Tabler scss files into one tabler-backpack.min.css and got much better results. I mean, MUCH BETTER. I am definitely happier with it than with the previous solution.

So what?
Well, now we have 2 complete css files: the one provided by Tabler with original colors (light and dark modes), and our css with Backpack colors (light and dark).

My question is... can we, based on config.useBackpackColorSkin, load one correct css file?

So far, we were always loading https://unpkg.com/@tabler/core@1.0.0-beta17/dist/css/tabler.min.css and on top adding backpack-colors.css.

This is what I imagine (tested it, and it works fine):

@if(config(useBackpackColorSkin))
    @basset(base_path('vendor/backpack/theme-tabler/resources/assets/css/tabler-backpack.min.css')) // this can be hosted by Backpack and not included in the repo?
@else
    @basset('https://unpkg.com/@tabler/core@1.0.0-beta17/dist/css/tabler.min.css') // this is the original css file provided by Tabler with original colors
@endif

@basset(base_path('vendor/backpack/theme-tabler/resources/assets/css/tabler-adjustments.css')) // adjustments always needed regardless of Backpack skin.
@basset(base_path('vendor/backpack/crud/src/resources/assets/css/common.css'))

What do you think? 🤔

